   "exports": [],
   "body": "## Goal\nSession #175 landed 11 public development cases (`benchmark/cases/dev/`, generator `benchmark/scripts/dev_cases.py`, authored in #170 and verified in #175, both by codex/gpt-6.1-sol). `tasks` and `oracle` stay `prepared-not-reviewed` until an independent review checks them against the original artifacts. Expected gain: the first independent claim-level agreement rate for the development keys, plus concrete defects, so that the next Policymaker can either order fixes or record the review as evidence toward `tasks`/`oracle` review. The next Policymaker reads this report for: the reviewed commit, the per-family sample sizes, the counts of agreements and disagreements, and the list of findings.\n\n## Acceptance\n- [ ] Record the reviewed commit (`git rev-parse HEAD`) and the model you actually ran on. If you are not a Claude model, say so: in that case the review has no model-family diversity.\n- [ ] Independent re-extraction: write your own stdlib script under `.session/artifacts/` (do not import or copy `dev_cases.py`). It reads originals from `$LABVIEW_ENVIRONMENT` (/resources/environment), resolves each sampled locator (e.g. `/Project/Item[1]/Item[2]/@URL`, `text()/utf8-sha256`) and compares the value with the case's reference value. Sample deterministically: every claim of `vi-actor-core-native-gap` and `library-specialty`, plus at least 20 claims per remaining case chosen by a fixed seed. Report agree/disagree/unresolvable counts per family.\n- [ ] Check the artifact sha256 of every case against the original file (or archive member) bytes yourself.\n- [ ] Spec checks against `benchmark/protocol.md` `## tasks` and `## oracle`: native-required claims (dependency resolution, inheritance, dispatch, diagrams, behaviour) are never asserted from XML; denominators include unavailable references; the lineage group ids are consistent across copies/variants (protocol `## split`, first two paragraphs); questions resemble real tasks from the goal (computation, dependencies, typedef impact, diagram differences) or the gap is stated.\n- [ ] Separate Standards and Spec findings, each with path, locator, evidence, impact and correction. End with an overall recommendation for this commit: accept as development evidence / revise / reject.\n- [ ] No fixes and no repository changes (the profile has none). No readiness, threshold, scope-reduction or LabVIEW 2024 claim.\n## Verification\n`python3 -I benchmark/scripts/dev_cases.py --check`\n## Context\n- `benchmark/cases/dev/README.md` (6 KB): case format, locator syntax, and section `## Review next`.\n- `benchmark/protocol.md`: read only sections `## tasks`, `## oracle`, and the first two paragraphs of `## split` (the file is 38 KB).\n- `docs/perpetua/evaluation.md`: read as the reviewer skill requires.\n## Budget\nPrevious sessions died at the 800k input ceiling. Case JSON files are 12-544 KB, and `sources.json`/`coverage.json` are large: never Read or print them whole. Use `python3 -I` one-liners that print counts, keys or single claims. Do not read engine code, history, research or `resources-proposal.md`. Write `.session/report.md` early and update it after each measured step, so that a budget stop still leaves the counts.",
