   "exports": [],
   "body": "## Goal\nThe protocol's `## split` milestone is `not-started`. Its first ready step works on public sources only: group copies and variants into lineage groups before any allocation. Expected gain: a reproducible public lineage inventory (exact duplicates by original/archive-member hash, plus candidate variants that still need adjudication) that moves `split` to partial preparation without any private data. The next Policymaker checks the exit codes of the two verification commands, the counts of groups and candidates, and whether the inventory agrees with the `lineage_group_id` values already used in `benchmark/cases/dev/`.\n\n## Acceptance\n- [ ] Write a stdlib script `benchmark/scripts/lineage.py` (generate plus `--check`, in the style of `benchmark/scripts/dev_cases.py`: no importing or executing prepared code, and preflight before writing). It reads `$LABVIEW_ENVIRONMENT` and the hashes already pinned in `benchmark/sources.json`/`coverage.json`.\n- [ ] Output `benchmark/lineage.json`: (a) exact-copy groups by sha256 across all repositories and archive members; (b) candidate variants (same relative name or same LabVIEW qualified name with different hashes, or different save versions) marked `candidate-unadjudicated`; (c) a map from each dev case's `lineage_group_id` to its members; (d) remaining uncertainty and the method. Hash inequality must not be treated as independence.\n- [ ] Add a short `benchmark/lineage.md` summary (counts only, no case keys). Pin the new files as `split` evidence in `benchmark/preparation.json` per the pinning rule in `execution/roles/benchmark/SKILL.md`. In `benchmark/preparation-status.json` keep `split` at `not-started` (the restricted allocation and isolation evidence do not exist yet) and record the public lineage inventory as prepared, unreviewed preparation in its limitations text.\n- [ ] State explicitly what is still missing for `split`: a restricted store, a custodian, private/new cases, native structural comparison and tested isolation. No allocation into evaluation partitions, no readiness claim, no product code.\n## Verification\n`python3 -I policy/evaluator/evaluate.py --check`\n## Context\n- `benchmark/protocol.md`: read only section `## split`.\n- `execution/roles/benchmark/SKILL.md`: pinning rule.\n- `benchmark/scripts/dev_cases.py`: read its first ~80 lines only for the pin and preflight idiom.\n## Budget\nEarlier sessions died at the 800k input ceiling. Never Read or print `sources.json`, `coverage.json` or case JSON whole: use `python3 -I` one-liners with counts and keys. Do not print `lineage.json` whole once it is written. Do not read engine code, history or research. Write `.session/report.md` first and update it after each command. If the budget runs short, commit a working generator with `--check` before attempting variant heuristics.",
